{"title":"2011 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Nine hundred forty-three minus eighty-seven equals\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/d/66dda2e908cc0c228d90b9a1b2f747808436b9ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ -1030 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ -856 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 770 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 1030 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 856$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"541\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can find each number in numerical form and then subtract them.\n</p><p>Nine hundred forty-three in numerical form would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abbe7f4608fbd8f734a9722978df37a0bbbbd34a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$943$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, while eighty-seven in numerical form would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/1/711f5fc6f8d53d2565cff62b15f932f02e0dbc58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$87$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>Subtracting these, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/b/1eb8cb29dabb70b30d0aa6ec91cad0490f3a096f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$943 - 87 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(E) } 856}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"166\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Pascal\" title=\"2011 CEMC Pascal\">2011 CEMC Pascal</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Pascal_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2011 CEMC Pascal Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Pascal_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2011 CEMC Pascal Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2011 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2011 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2011 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2011 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2011 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2011 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 5\"